###user api requests
GET http://localhost:3000/user-api/users 

### here user is the resource name the only data is between client and server is json data

POST http://localhost:3000/user-api/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "id": 100,
  "name": "Anu",
  "age":21
}  


### only put and post request have body data and get and delete request do not have body data
### url has the parameter also

PUT http://localhost:3000/user-api/users/100
#why we have put 100? because we are modifying user with id 100
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "id": 100,
  "name": "Anu updated",
  "age":22
}  
### Read a user by id-in form of url parameters
GET http://localhost:3000/user-api/users/100

###
DELETE http://localhost:3000/user-api/users/100







